      D = 10 :  n = D(D-3)/2 = 35
      D = 11 :  n = D(D-3)/2 = 44
  [PASS] N1 [THE VALUE] at D = 4 the count is exactly 2 -- the SPARC mode count
         measured: n(4) = 4(4-3)/2 = 2
         This is the derivation: the integer the programme measured in the
         slope of mu_2 is the standard transverse-polarization count of
         a massless spin-2 field in four dimensions.
  [PASS] N2 [UNIQUENESS] D(D-3)/2 = 2 has roots D = 4 and D = -1 only; D = -1 is
      unphysical, so n = 2 SELECTS D = 4 with no freedom
         measured: integer roots of D^2 - 3D - 4 = 0 in [-5, 20): [-1, 4]
         This is what makes it a derivation rather than a fit: the value is
         forced, and the unphysical root is discarded by D > 0.
  [PASS] N3 [BOUNDARY] D = 3 gives n = 0, matching the fact that gravity in 2+1
